  "decision": "For an idle, dedicated RX 7900 XTX, 114,688 total context tokens is the highest completed Qwen3.8-27B pure-INT8 c1 row; four different pinned ShareGPT-derived requests passed with exact accounting, zero leaked ownership, 23.322876 GiB peak, and 0.661499 GiB headroom. At c2, every tested row through 6,144 tokens/request completed, while 8,192 failed both requests with HIP OOM and 8,448 failed startup because direct no-mirror packed INT8 is unsupported. Physical c4 completed 1,536/request for 16/16 multi-turn requests, and no c4 execution failure was tested. Shape-aware offered-c8 rows execute as two physical c4 waves; offered c8 completed every tested row through 2,048/request, although that highest raw row predates shape capture, and no c8 execution failure was observed. The short c>1 route retains a BF16 mirror and is not an efficient INT8 capacity path.",
